-- title:
--   Flat p-adic Galois representation attached to a weight-two Hecke eigensystem, p ∤ N
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime, $N \geq 1$ an integer and $S$ a finite set of natural numbers with $p \in S$ and containing every prime divisor of $N$. Let $\mathcal{O}'$ be a complete discrete valuation domain of characteristic zero with finite residue field in which $p$ lies in the maximal ideal, and let $\chi$ be a ring homomorphism from [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 S`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) — the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $\operatorname{End}_{\mathbb{C}}$ of weight-two cusp forms for $\Gamma_0(N)$ generated by the operators $T_\ell$ for primes $\ell \nmid N$, $\ell \notin S$ together with the operators $U_q$ for primes $q \mid N$, $q \notin S$ — to $\mathcal{O}'$. Assume $p \nmid N$. Then there is a complete discrete valuation domain $\mathcal{O}''$ of characteristic zero with finite residue field, which is a module-finite local $\mathcal{O}'$-algebra with injective structure map, and a [`GaloisRepAdic 𝒪''`](def/GaloisRep_Adic.html#L16), that is, a free $\mathcal{O}''$-module $V$ of rank $2$ with a monoid homomorphism $\rho$ from $\operatorname{Aut}_{\mathbb{Q}}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}})$ to $\operatorname{End}_{\mathcal{O}''}(V)$ that is continuous for the adic filtration (each $\rho(\sigma)$ acts trivially modulo $\mathfrak{m}^n V$ for $\sigma$ fixing a suitable finite extension of $\mathbb{Q}$), such that: (i) for every prime $\ell$ with $\ell \nmid N$ and $\ell \notin S$, every valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $\ell$ a nonunit of $A$, and every $\sigma$ in the decomposition subgroup of $A$ acting as $x \mapsto x^{\ell}$ on the residue field of $A$, the characteristic polynomial of $\rho(\sigma)$ is $X^2 - \chi(T_\ell)X + \ell$, the image of $\chi(T_\ell)$ in $\mathcal{O}''$ being taken; and (ii) $\rho$ satisfies `IsFlatAt p`: the residue field of $\mathcal{O}''$ is finite and for every ideal $I$ of $\mathcal{O}''$ with $\mathcal{O}''/I$ finite there is a finite flat cocommutative Hopf algebra $H$ over the subring of rationals with denominator prime to $p$ and a bijection from the convolution group of $\mathbb{Z}_{(p)}$-algebra maps $H \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ onto $V/IV$ which is additive and equivariant for the induced action of $\operatorname{Aut}_{\mathbb{Q}}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}})$ on $V/IV$.
--
--   This is the existence, with flatness at $p$, of the $p$-adic Galois representation attached to a weight-two Hecke eigensystem of level $N$ in the case $p \nmid N$ (Eichler–Shimura–Deligne–Carayol), the flatness expressing that each finite quotient $V/IV$ comes from a finite flat commutative group scheme over $\mathbb{Z}_{(p)}$. It is used in the dichotomy results that, at primes dividing the level or where flatness fails, force strict ordinarity of the eigensystem, and in the sign statement for the operators $U_q$ at squarefree level.
